{#- The approval page: the one place a scope is granted, and the press design.md §12
    ("The grant is one press, and chatting is included", 2026-09-24) rests on.

    It is the sign-in page's family — the lockup, one card on the desk, no navigation —
    because it is the same kind of moment: somebody is in the middle of something that
    started somewhere else, and a page with three ways off it would be three ways to
    lose them. It reuses `signin.css` and adds only the scope list.

    It grants what the app asked for, together, in one press. There are no ticks, and
    nothing here promises one. Two things are load-bearing rather than decorative. The
    client's name is the client's claim about itself, because dynamic registration means
    a stranger wrote it, so the host the reader goes back to stands in bold beside the
    press. And the spending scope says that chatting is included, because a message
    rounds to no credits at all (§12, 2026-09-23).

    Drawn as board ConnApprove since 2026-10-09 (design.md §12, "The connector's pages
    are the boards'"): who is signed in, with Not you?; a glyph for each scope; the well
    with what the month has left; Connect and Not now on one line. -#}
<!doctype html>
<html lang="{{ page_language|default('en') }}">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>targum</title>
{% include '_icons.html.j2' %}
<style>{{ asset('tokens.css') }}{{ asset('shared.css') }}{{ asset('signin.css') }}</style>
{{ hebrew_face() }}
{{ chrome_face() }}
</head>
<body class="signin">
<main class="gate">
  <a class="brand" href="/" aria-label="targum">
    <svg class="brand-mark" viewBox="20 12 56 72" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
      <rect x="20" y="12" width="22" height="62" rx="5" fill="currentColor"></rect>
      <rect x="54" y="22" width="22" height="62" rx="5" fill="var(--mark-accent)"></rect>
    </svg>
    <span>targum</span>
  </a>

  <div class="door grant">
    {#- Who is granting (design.md §12, "The connector's pages are the boards'",
        2026-10-09; board ConnApprove): the address, and Not you?, which signs out and
        comes back to this same request, so nobody grants on somebody else's account. -#}
    <form class="who" method="post" action="/oauth/authorize">
      <input type="hidden" name="asked" value="{{ query }}">
      <span class="who-letter" aria-hidden="true">{{ (email or "?")[:1]|upper }}</span>
      <span class="who-says">{{ t("connect.page.signed-in-as", "Signed in as {address}", address=email) }}</span>
      <button class="who-not" type="submit" name="press" value="not-you">{{ t("connect.page.not-you", "Not you?") }}</button>
    </form>
    <h1>{{ t("connect.page.connect-to-targum", "Connect {client} to targum", client=client or t("connect.page.this-app", "this app")) }}</h1>
    <p class="said">{{ t("connect.page.it-will-be-able-to", "It will be able to:") }}</p>

    <ul class="scopes grant-scopes">
      {%- for scope in scopes %}
      {#- Through the catalogue, not straight off `oauth.SCOPES`. The three scopes are
          written in that module as English and were drawn here raw, so a Russian
          reader met the whole page in their own language except the three lines that
          say what they are agreeing to (2026-09-23). `tests/test_oauth.py` holds the
          English here and there to the same words. -#}
      <li>
        <span class="scope-glyph" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 16 16" focusable="false">
          {%- if scope.name == 'library' %}<circle cx="7" cy="7" r="4.2"/><path d="M10.2 10.2 13.5 13.5"/>
          {%- elif scope.name == 'record' %}<path d="M3 4.5h10M3 8h7M3 11.5h4"/>
          {%- else %}<path d="M2.5 3.5h11v7h-6l-3 2.5v-2.5h-2z"/>{% endif -%}
        </svg></span>
        <span class="scope-says">{{ t("connect.scope." + scope.name, scope.says) }}
          {%- if scope.name == 'chat' %}<small>{{ t("connect.scope.chat-also", "And add texts to your playlists, and offer texts, playlists and subscriptions, which you confirm here, on targum") }}</small>{% endif %}</span>
      </li>
      {%- endfor %}
    </ul>

    {%- if spends %}
    {#- Said once, in a well above the press: that talking costs nothing to count, what
        does use credits and where it is confirmed, what the month has left, and what the
        grant lets targum keep. -#}
    <div class="grant-well">
      <p><b>{{ t("connect.page.chatting-is-included-sentence", "Chatting is included.") }}</b></p>
      <p>{{ t("connect.page.uses-credits-once-confirmed", "A text, playlist or subscription uses credits only once you confirm it here.") }}
        {%- if left is not none %} {{ tn("connect.page.credits-left", left, "You have {n} credit left this month, about {clock} of audio.", "You have {n} credits left this month, about {clock} of audio.", clock=clock) }}{% endif %}</p>
      <p class="grant-keep">{{ t("connect.page.we-keep-the-lines", "We keep the lines we correct, and add that language to the ones you're learning.") }}</p>
    </div>
    {%- endif %}

    {#- Where the press sends the reader, beside the press and at body size: the heading
        says what the app calls itself, and this says where it actually lives. -#}
    <p class="said dest">{{ t("connect.page.then-we-ll-send-you-back-to", "Then we'll send you back to {host}.", host=host) }}</p>

    <form class="grant-press" method="post" action="/oauth/authorize">
      <input type="hidden" name="asked" value="{{ query }}">
      <button class="btn filled go" type="submit" name="press" value="approve"><span class="go-says">{{ t("connect.page.connect", "Connect") }}</span><svg class="go-arrow" viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M3 8h10M9 4l4 4-4 4"/></svg></button>
      <button class="ghost" type="submit" name="press" value="refuse">{{ t("connect.page.not-now", "Not now") }}</button>
    </form>

    <p class="aside">{{ t("connect.page.you-can-disconnect-it-later", "You can disconnect it from your account at any time.") }}</p>
  </div>
</main>
</body>
</html>
